{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dt7ShJdtDuLrmrkfRf8fc1","type":"tool_result","content":"296\t    # \"absence ⇒ fail-closed\" inversion (C10): that would need a\n297\t    # definition of \"expected\" which is itself editable, and would make\n298\t    # DELETING a file the way to choose the posture.\n299\t    \".claude/security/sentinel-signers-registry.yaml\",\n300\t    \".claude/policies/.drift-manifest.json\",\n301\t    # KERNEL-DECOMPOSITION (v1.4.4 train, merge 888e9e6c). These rows\n302\t    # cover the code the v1.4.4 split moved out of seven kernel facades,\n303\t    # the plan-path predicate the train put in place of regexes in two\n304\t    # kernel files, and the modules listed below that kernel code calls.\n305\t    #   - Seven facades moved their code into helper packages. One recursive\n306\t    #     row per package makes that code HARD-DENY again, as it was inside\n307\t    #     the facades in v1.4.2, and a file added there later is HARD-DENY\n308\t    #     too (the federation-dir precedent above).\n309\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/**/*\",  # check_canonical_edit.py\n310\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/**/*\",  # check_agent_spawn.py\n311\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_policy_parts/**/*\",  # _lib/policy.py\n312\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*\",  # _lib/audit_emit.py\n313\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts/**/*\",  # audit_log.py\n314\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/**/*\",  # check_bash_safety.py\n315\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_pair_rail_parts/**/*\",  # check_pair_rail.py\n316\t    #   - Five flat modules that kernel code calls:\n317\t    #     plan_paths.py — the plan-path predicate (is_plan_path,\n318\t    #       plan_id_from_path) that replaces the plan-path regexes the train\n319\t    #       removed from check_plan_edit.py and policy_preprocessors.py; it\n320\t    #       is HARD-DENY again, as those regexes were in v1.4.2;\n321\t    #     model_currency.py — is_veto_floor_model(), the VETO-floor predicate\n322\t    #       that kernel files now call as part of their VETO-floor check\n323\t    #       (the F-01-03 demotion check above rides on it);\n324\t    #     cli_currency.py, bash_indirect_guard.py, bash_indirect_telemetry.py\n325\t    #       — each added by this train and called by kernel code:\n326\t    #       cli_currency.py is the Codex payload-pin currency arm, which\n327\t    #       decides whether a payload SHA mismatch is accepted as\n328\t    #       \"compatible\" (called by the pair-rail code; ADR-182 trust root);\n329\t    #       bash_indirect_guard.py is the indirect-command BLOCK matcher and\n330\t    #       bash_indirect_telemetry.py the disabled-rail telemetry, both\n331\t    #       called by the bash-safety parts.\n332\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/model_currency.py\",\n333\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/cli_currency.py\",\n334\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/plan_paths.py\",\n335\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py\",\n336\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_telemetry.py\",\n337\t    #   - adapters/live/ — the live-adapter transport package, present since\n338\t    #     v1.0.0 and enrolled now because the kernel adapters/__init__.py\n339\t    #     loads it; its siblings above are already kernel.\n340\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/adapters/live/**/*\",\n341\t    # tests/test_kernel_decomposition_coverage.py checks that each package\n342\t    # below _lib/ that a kernel source reaches by an import statement or\n343\t    # by a / chain of string literals (resolved against the source's\n344\t    # directory or .claude/hooks) is kernel in full, and that each of the\n345\t    # five flat modules above is kernel and still imported by a kernel"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6cb4051e-a398-43c8-941a-d1137bf30aab","uuid":"757036ec-ba10-440c-8858-0fc530cf85f7","timestamp":"2026-11-15T10:02:48.175Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9sr